omni-voice - A comprehensive development toolkit

A comprehensive development toolkit

Usage: omni-voice [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  capture        Captures audio from a microphone to a 16 kHz mono WAV file
  transcribe     Transcribes a 16 kHz mono WAV file to JSONL or markdown
  reflect        Reflects on a transcript and emits reflection events
  listen         Listens on a live microphone, transcribing and reflecting continuously
  review         Reconciles a session's events.jsonl into materialized markdown
  install-model  Downloads the model files for a chosen variant (Whisper tiny.en for the `whisper-candle` backend, or wespeaker for speaker embedding) into `~/.omni-voice/voice/models/<variant>/`
  enroll         Captures a microphone sample and persists a speaker embedding to `~/.omni-voice/voice/speakers/<name>.json`
  help-all       Displays comprehensive help for all commands
  help           Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --ai-backend <AI_BACKEND>
          Selects the AI backend used by commands that invoke an AI model [possible values: default, claude-cli]
      --claude-cli-allow-tools
          Weakens the `claude-cli` sandbox by allowing the nested `claude -p` session to use its default built-in tools (Read, Edit, Write, Bash, Glob, Grep)
      --claude-cli-allow-mcp
          Weakens the `claude-cli` sandbox by allowing the nested `claude -p` session to load MCP servers from `~/.claude/settings.json`
      --claude-cli-max-budget-usd <AMOUNT>
          Per-invocation spending cap in USD for the `claude-cli` backend
      --models-yaml <PATH>
          Path to a single user-side `models.yaml` that short-circuits the standard `./.omni-voice/models.yaml` and `~/.omni-voice/models.yaml` lookup. The file is still merged over the embedded catalog. Equivalent to setting `OMNI_VOICE_MODELS_YAML`
  -h, --help
          Print help (see more with '--help')
  -V, --version
          Print version


================================================================================

omni-voice capture - Captures audio from a microphone to a 16 kHz mono WAV file

Captures audio from a microphone to a 16 kHz mono WAV file

Usage: capture [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --idle-after <IDLE_AFTER>  Stop after this many seconds of trailing silence. `0` disables auto-stop — capture runs until Ctrl-C [default: 5]
      --output <OUTPUT>          Destination WAV path. Defaults to `~/.omni-voice/voice/captures/<UTC-timestamp>.wav`
      --device <DEVICE>          Audio input device name. Defaults to the system default input. Matching is exact against the platform-reported device name; an unknown name errors with a list of detected devices
  -h, --help                     Print help


================================================================================

omni-voice completions - Generates shell completion scripts

Generates shell completion scripts

Usage: completions <SHELL>

Arguments:
  <SHELL>  Target shell (`bash`, `elvish`, `fish`, `powershell`, `zsh`) [possible values: bash, elvish, fish, powershell, zsh]

Options:
  -h, --help  Print help


================================================================================

omni-voice enroll - Captures a microphone sample and persists a speaker embedding to `~/.omni-voice/voice/speakers/<name>.json`

Captures a microphone sample and persists a speaker embedding to `~/.omni-voice/voice/speakers/<name>.json`

Usage: enroll [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --name <NAME>                    Identifier under which to store the embedding (the JSON filename stem). Defaults to `default` [default: default]
      --idle-after <IDLE_AFTER>        Stop after this many seconds of trailing silence [default: 2]
      --max-secs <MAX_SECS>            Hard upper bound on capture duration in seconds. Capture stops as soon as this many seconds have elapsed, even if speech continues. `0` disables the cap (only idle/Ctrl-C will stop the capture) [default: 30]
      --device <DEVICE>                Audio input device name. Defaults to the system default input
      --speaker-model <SPEAKER_MODEL>  Path to the wespeaker ONNX model. Overrides the default at `~/.omni-voice/voice/models/wespeaker-en-voxceleb-resnet34-LM/` and the `OMNI_VOICE_VOICE_SPEAKER_MODEL` env var
      --force                          Overwrite an existing `<name>.json` enrolment instead of refusing
  -h, --help                           Print help


================================================================================

omni-voice help-all - Displays comprehensive help for all commands

Displays comprehensive help for all commands

Usage: help-all

Options:
  -h, --help  Print help


================================================================================

omni-voice install-model - Downloads the model files for a chosen variant (Whisper tiny.en for the `whisper-candle` backend, or wespeaker for speaker embedding) into `~/.omni-voice/voice/models/<variant>/`

Downloads the model files for a chosen variant (Whisper tiny.en for the `whisper-candle` backend, or wespeaker for speaker embedding) into `~/.omni-voice/voice/models/<variant>/`

Usage: install-model [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --dest <DEST>        Override the install directory. Defaults to the variant's canonical location under `~/.omni-voice/voice/models/`
      --force              Re-download even if all required files are already present
      --accept-downloads   Proceed with downloads without the interactive confirmation prompt. Also bypassable via `OMNI_VOICE_AUTO_DOWNLOAD=true` for non-interactive automation (CI)
      --variant <VARIANT>  Which model variant to install. Defaults to `whisper-tiny.en` [default: whisper-tiny.en] [possible values: whisper-tiny.en, parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v2, voxtral-mlx-int4, speaker-wespeaker-en]
  -h, --help               Print help (see more with '--help')


================================================================================

omni-voice listen - Listens on a live microphone, transcribing and reflecting continuously

Listens on a live microphone, transcribing and reflecting continuously

Usage: listen [OPTIONS] --session <SESSION>

Options:
      --session <SESSION>
          Session id. Transcript, events, and logs live under `~/.omni-voice/voice/<id>/`
      --backend <BACKEND>
          ASR backend. Must be a streaming backend (`voxtral-mlx` or `mock`); batch backends are rejected. Defaults to the build's streaming default
      --device <DEVICE>
          Audio input device name. Defaults to the system default input
      --audio-buffer-size <AUDIO_BUFFER_SIZE>
          cpal capture buffer size in frames (100 ms at 16 kHz by default) [default: 1600]
      --trigger-silence-gap-ms <TRIGGER_SILENCE_GAP_MS>
          Reflect after this many milliseconds of silence [default: 1500]
      --trigger-word-delta <TRIGGER_WORD_DELTA>
          Reflect after this many finalized words since the last reflection [default: 30]
      --trigger-max-interval-ms <TRIGGER_MAX_INTERVAL_MS>
          Reflect at least this often (milliseconds) during unbroken speech [default: 60000]
      --idle-after <IDLE_AFTER>
          Auto-stop after this many seconds of continuous silence. `0` (default) runs until Ctrl-C [default: 0]
      --speaker <SPEAKER>
          Lock onto an enrolled speaker: only speech matching this speaker's voice is transcribed; other voices in the room are dropped. Requires a prior `omni-voice enroll --name <name>`. Omit to transcribe everyone
      --speaker-threshold <SPEAKER_THRESHOLD>
          Cosine-similarity threshold for `--speaker`. Defaults to 0.5; higher is stricter. Ignored unless `--speaker` is set
      --speaker-model <SPEAKER_MODEL>
          Path to the wespeaker ONNX model. Overrides the default at `~/.omni-voice/voice/models/wespeaker-en-voxceleb-resnet34-LM/` and `OMNI_VOICE_VOICE_SPEAKER_MODEL`. Ignored unless `--speaker` is set
  -h, --help
          Print help


================================================================================

omni-voice reflect - Reflects on a transcript and emits reflection events

Reflects on a transcript and emits reflection events

Usage: reflect [OPTIONS] [TRANSCRIPT]

Arguments:
  [TRANSCRIPT]  Path to a `transcript.jsonl` file. Pass `-` for stdin. Omit to fall back to `--session` or stdin

Options:
      --session <SESSION>  Reflect against a named voice session under `~/.omni-voice/voice/<id>/`. Mutually exclusive with a positional transcript path
  -h, --help               Print help


================================================================================

omni-voice review - Reconciles a session's events.jsonl into materialized markdown

Reconciles a session's events.jsonl into materialized markdown

Usage: review [OPTIONS] <SESSION_ID>

Arguments:
  <SESSION_ID>  Session id under `~/.omni-voice/voice/<id>/`

Options:
      --what <WHAT>  Which artefact to materialise. `all` (default) writes both markdown files and applies the TTL pass. `transcript` renders `transcript.jsonl` to stdout instead [default: all] [possible values: transcript, todos, decisions, all]
  -h, --help         Print help (see more with '--help')


================================================================================

omni-voice transcribe - Transcribes a 16 kHz mono WAV file to JSONL or markdown

Transcribes a 16 kHz mono WAV file to JSONL or markdown

Usage: transcribe [OPTIONS] <WAV>

Arguments:
  <WAV>  Path to a 16 kHz mono 16-bit PCM WAV file. Use `capture` to produce one — `transcribe` does not resample

Options:
      --backend <BACKEND>              Transcriber backend (`mock`, `whisper-candle`, `whisper-candle-streaming`, `parakeet-tdt`). Defaults to `mock`; see ADR-0033 for the `whisper-candle` runtime choice, ADR-0040 for the latency-tolerant streaming variant, and ADR-0042 / #23 for the pure-Rust Parakeet-TDT backend
      --model <MODEL>                  Path to a backend-specific model directory. For `whisper-candle` and `whisper-candle-streaming`, this overrides `OMNI_VOICE_VOICE_WHISPER_MODEL` and the default at `~/.omni-voice/voice/models/whisper-tiny.en/`. Ignored by `mock`
      --format <FORMAT>                Output format. Defaults to `md` on a tty, `jsonl` when piped [possible values: jsonl, md]
      --speaker <SPEAKER>              Enrolled speaker to filter on. Drops any `Final` event whose segment doesn't match the enrolled embedding by cosine similarity at or above `--threshold`
      --threshold <THRESHOLD>          Cosine-similarity threshold for `--speaker`. Defaults to 0.5; see [`DEFAULT_SPEAKER_THRESHOLD`]
      --speaker-model <SPEAKER_MODEL>  Path to the wespeaker ONNX model. Overrides the default at `~/.omni-voice/voice/models/wespeaker-en-voxceleb-resnet34-LM/` and `OMNI_VOICE_VOICE_SPEAKER_MODEL`. Ignored unless `--speaker` is set
  -h, --help                           Print help (see more with '--help')
